  "_comment": [
    "Domain-family filter (v2 pre-step). A job is KEPT when its work belongs to any",
    "family below; otherwise it is ELIMINATED before any resume work starts.",
    "Families: software, ai_data, automation, hardware_iot, finance.",
    "tech_business_direct terms are self-sufficient (ERP/CRM/HRIS/SaaS = tech angle).",
    "tech_business_needs_tech terms count ONLY when another family also signals",
    "(business administration + AI/software/automation = keep; pure business = out).",
    "out_identity keys mark other-domain jobs (mechanical/civil/health/hospitality...).",
    "A job is eliminated when its TITLE carries an out_identity key and no family",
    "keyword, or when out-identity clearly dominates (out>=2 and family<=1).",
    "",
    "SCORED MODE (default): family-less jobs get one more chance - they are kept",
    "when >= scoring.min_skill_alignment (0.60) of their demanded skills are skills",
    "the candidate is licensed to claim. Demands are discovered from the JD text:",
    "KB skills/aliases + GENERIC_SYNONYMS (code) match; demand_tools below are",
    "demanded-but-unclaimable. A degree requirement counts once (matched when a",
    "candidate degree field is named). industry_keywords add a bounded bonus for",
    "tech-adjacent employers. Edit words/numbers here to tune - no code changes.",
    "--loose-filter on run_step4.py restores keyword-only mode."
